Data sources (each used with the user's own API key and under that service's terms of use)
- BrickLink (https://www.bricklink.com): set details, images, parts lists and sold prices.
- Rebrickable (https://rebrickable.com): themes, minifigure counts and alternate builds.
- Brickset (https://brickset.com): original retail prices and launch and retirement dates.
- LDraw (https://www.ldraw.org): the LDraw Parts Library and models from the Official Model Repository,
  licensed CC BY 2.0 by the LDraw.org contributors. Each model's author is shown under the 3D view.
  The test fixtures in lib/ldraw/fixtures are simplified stand-ins.

Bundled software
- three.js (MIT) for the 3D view.
- Lucide icons (ISC), which include icons from Feather (MIT).
- Archivo by Omnibus-Type (SIL Open Font License 1.1), self-hosted through next/font.
- sharp and libvips (Apache-2.0 and LGPL-3.0-or-later), used by Next.js image optimization in the Docker image.
  libvips is dynamically linked; its source is at https://github.com/libvips/libvips.
- Next.js, React, Drizzle ORM, SQLite (public domain) through better-sqlite3, and the other packages listed
  with their licenses in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
